  squares:
    count: 1-7 total; 0-3 grey + 0-4 pink, at least 1 of either
    shape: solid 3x3 of a single color (grey or pink)
    placement: non-overlapping; min gap >=1 cell between any two square bboxes
    may touch grid boundary (markers never on boundary-blocked sides)
  markers:
    color: maroon (9), single pixels in cells orthogonally adjacent to exactly one square
    per_square: 1-5 markers across 1-3 sides; each side has 1-3 of 3 possible slots filled
    each marker touches exactly one square (no ambiguity)
    pink_projection: each pink-adjacent marker is handled independently. Left/right-side markers stamp the square's middle column at the marker's row; above/below-side markers stamp the square's middle row at the marker's column. A marker centered on its side therefore stamps the square center. Multiple markers from any sides simply union their projected cells; there is no side priority.
  transform:
    grey_squares: erased to background; markers stay in place and stamp the nearest edge cell of the former square (same row for left/right, same col for above/below)
    pink_squares: preserved; adjacent markers are removed, then replaced by the union of independent centerline projections according to pink_projection

